Development tooling
-------------------

Everything under `tools/` -- the PowerShell harness and scenario scripts, the
packer, the release gate, the git hooks, and the two devbridge addons -- is
original work of this project. The directory is the list; adding a file there
adds it to this statement.

Copyright (C) 2026 SkoobyDoo <skoobot.reclauded@proton.me>

None of it is adapted from Tales of Maj'Eyal, Player AI, SkooBot, or mishander's
fork. It carries no other author's copyright header, and the attribution chain
above does not apply to it. Sole authorship is recorded here deliberately: GPL-3.0
is only enforceable by someone who can show they hold the copyright, and this is
what makes that provable.

It is licensed GPL-3.0, the same as the rest of this repository. The PowerShell
harness is an external process driver, not a derivative of the game, so it could
have been licensed permissively. GPL-3.0 is a deliberate choice rather than an
inherited obligation: the intent is that improvements stay available to everyone
who receives them, and that the work cannot be folded into a closed product.

The two devbridge addons are development-only. They execute arbitrary Lua from
disk by design, are never packaged into a release (see T-035), and should not be
installed by anyone who is not developing this addon.


On the name
-----------

"Reclauded" is a play on "rebooted". This addon was built with the assistance
of Claude, an AI assistant made by Anthropic.

It contains no language model and makes no network requests. It runs entirely
offline inside the game, as ordinary Lua. No API key is required and no data
leaves your machine. Claude's involvement is authorship, not architecture.

Claude is a trademark of Anthropic, PBC. This project is not affiliated with,
endorsed by, or sponsored by Anthropic.

Tales of Maj'Eyal is a trademark of Nicolas Casalini. This project is not
affiliated with or endorsed by the ToME developers.
